-story"><p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/nyc/">New York</a> / <a href="/nyc/projects/">VG projects</a></p><p class="eyebrow">VISION GRAPHICS PORTFOLIO</p><h1>Café Rio: coordinated graphics for restaurants and delivery fleets</h1><div class="project-story-grid"><figure><img src="/nyc/assets/vg-project-cafe-rio.webp" alt="Café Rio branded delivery vans parked together outside a Vision Graphics facility" width="1280" height="720"><figcaption>Café Rio fleet graphics from the Vision Graphics portfolio. Photographed location not specified.</figcaption></figure><div><h2>What VG delivered</h2><p class="lead">Vision Graphics worked with Café Rio on repeatable interior graphics, digital displays and branded delivery van graphics. A dedicated ordering portal organizes approved graphics, uniforms, packaging and other materials, supported by account management and fulfillment. The program is designed to keep the brand consistent as stores open, campaigns change and materials need replenishing. The photograph shows a group of Café Rio branded vans.</p><p>The photograph demonstrates fleet branding; it is not a storefront, window-graphics or restaurant-interior installation photo.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.visiondoesit.com/2025/12/cafe-rio-case-study/">Read the full VG case study <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a></div></div><div class="project-next"><div><h2>Bring the relevant ideas to your project.</h2><p>Send your location, photographs, approximate dimensions and target date. We’ll discuss the materials, design and delivery or installation arrangements for your own space.</p></div><a class="btn primary" href="/nyc/contact/?product=Caf%C3%A9%20Rio%20project%20inspiration">Discuss your project <svg xml